From 38e4480d8596a1da7949a390ca3a005ce3b46de4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Sat, 16 May 2026 12:43:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] perf phase 11 patch 0153 -- wave-57 Track B B2:
 FIXED_TIMESTEP accumulator + 3 screen-effect wart fixes

Per flush-instr's docs/internal/PHASE11-WAVE-57-CONTRACT.md. Wave-57 is
Track B's second wave (B2 in FIXED-TIMESTEP-DESIGN.md sec.3-4): the
fixed-timestep accumulator behind SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_FIXED_TIMESTEP,
built on the wave-56 tick_state() / tick_render_submit() split. Opt-in,
default-OFF; FIXED_TIMESTEP=0 is byte-identical to wave-56 (production).

WHY DOS NEEDS THIS: Cave Story logic is authored for GAME_FPS=50.
DOSKUTSU couples logic 1:1 to render, so at the faithful ~30 fps render
on g2k the game runs at ~60% speed -- it feels slow. The accumulator
runs game logic at a fixed 50 Hz off a wall-clock accumulator,
decoupled from render fps, so the game plays at correct authored speed
even at 30 fps render. This is a game-SPEED fix, NOT a render-fps lever
-- the fps counter still reads ~30; what changes is that logic,
animation and timers advance at the intended rate.

THE ACCUMULATOR (main.cpp run_tick_fixed, contract sec.1.1): when
FIXED_TIMESTEP=1 AND mode==GM_NORMAL, gameloop() calls run_tick_fixed()
instead of the 1:1 run_tick(). It accumulates wall-clock elapsed and
runs a catch-up while-loop of tick_state() ONLY (+ input_poll + the TAS
hook per logic tick); tick_render_submit() + flip() run exactly ONCE
per displayed frame after the loop. MAX_CATCHUP=5 clamps the
spiral-of-death; an accumulator>MAX*TICK_NS resync drops stale backlog
(and absorbs re-entry from the 1:1 path). run_tick() is left UNTOUCHED
(it aliases the now file-scope g_tick_count via a reference, the only
1-line change) so the FIXED_TIMESTEP=0 path stays byte-identical;
run_tick_fixed() replicates run_tick()'s per-frame machinery rather
than refactoring it.

THE wave-36 FORECLOSURE (contract sec.2): wave-36 ran a fixed-timestep
over game.tick() (which submits drawcalls) -> N x ~17 ms drawcall work
-> -28 fps. Wave-57's catch-up loop body is tick_state() and nothing
that draws or flips -- tick_render_submit()/flip() are outside the
loop. The catch-up loop re-pays only ~1 ms of logic per extra tick.
Triple-gated: the wave-56 split (tick_state drawcall-free), the
loop-body structure, and the effect Tick()s being drawcall-free.

STOP-1 -- THE LATCH-FRESHNESS INVARIANT (contract sec.1.3, flush-instr
counter): the catch-up while-loop guards on game.mode==GM_NORMAL &&
!game.paused directly (NOT just the wave-56 dispatch latch -- a
sim-triggered setmode inside game_tick_normal_state mutates game.mode
AFTER the latch is set, so a latch-only check misses it). AND: a paused
frame MUST still run exactly one tick_state() so _tick_dispatch is
latched fresh to TD_PAUSED -- otherwise it stays stale at
TD_GM_NORMAL_SPLIT and tick_render_submit() runs game_tick_normal_render
instead of the pause OnTick (pause screen never appears, unpause never
processed, hang). run_tick_fixed() therefore: if paused -> exactly one
tick_state(), no catch-up; else -> the catch-up loop.

tick_count is the LOGIC-tick counter (contract sec.5 measurement
basis): incremented once per tick_state() in run_tick_fixed, so the
canonical PLAY.TAS auto-exits at logic-tick 2593 regardless of render
rate. Promoted from a run_tick() function-local static to file scope
(g_tick_count) so the 1:1 and accumulator paths share one monotonic
stream across mode transitions -- behavior-preserving for the 1:1 path
(a function-local and a file-scope static hold the identical value).

THE 3 SCREEN-EFFECT WART FIXES (contract sec.1.5): SE_FlashScreen,
SE_Starflash, SE_Fade each advanced animation state inside Draw().
Draw() runs in tick_render_submit() = render rate; under the
accumulator that would animate the effects ~1.67x slow at 30 fps.
SE_Fade is load-bearing, not cosmetic: game logic polls
fade.getstate() to sequence stage transitions (TRA) -- a render-rate
fade desyncs the transition logic. Fix: each effect's drawcall-free
state-advance is extracted to a Tick() method; under FIXED_TIMESTEP=1
Tick() runs in tick_state() (50 Hz, via the new block at the end of
Game::tick_state -- fade unconditional, flashscreen/starflash gated on
.enabled) and Draw() skips its embedded advance. Under FIXED_TIMESTEP=0
the advance stays in Draw() exactly as wave-56, behind an
if(!fixed_timestep_active()) guard -- so the OFF path is byte-identical
and needs NO prev-state snapshot (this supersedes the wave-56-contract
sec.3 prev-snapshot concern; the flag-gating avoids it).

STOP-2 -- SE_Starflash straddle (contract sec.1.5): SE_Starflash's
advance straddles its draw (speed/size advance before the fillRects,
state transition after). SE_Starflash::Tick() lifts the WHOLE advance
-- pre-advance then post-transition back-to-back (the fillRects touch
no speed/size/state, so back-to-back is state-math-equivalent to the
straddled order). Draw() keeps the original straddled code, each part
if(!fixed_timestep_active())-guarded, so FIXED_TIMESTEP=0 is
byte-identical (the else-branch early return included). On =1 the
one-tick phase shift is accepted per contract.

CORRECTNESS: FIXED_TIMESTEP=0 / unset -> run_tick_fixed() is never
called (the gameloop branch is false), run_tick() is untouched, and the
3 effects' Draw() advances run exactly as wave-56 -> byte-identical to
the wave-56 binary (build-qa tear-robust shared-subsequence AE=0 gate
vs sha c693499b). FIXED_TIMESTEP=1 is NOT byte-identity gated -- the
decoupled logic cadence IS the feature; it is verified by the wave-57
real-HW iter (the fixed-2593-logic-tick TAS run's wall-clock duration
~52 s at =1 vs ~86 s at =0, + render-fps non-regression = the wave-36
check).

BANNER for tests/run-gameplay-smoke.sh BANNERS:
"fixed-timestep: (ENABLED|DISABLED)" -- emitted on the first
fixed_timestep_active() call.

FILES: src/main.cpp (run_tick_fixed accumulator + the gameloop branch +
g_tick_count file-scope promotion + the run_tick alias), src/game.cpp
(fixed_timestep_active cached hint + the effect Tick() calls in
Game::tick_state), src/game.h (the decl), src/screeneffect.cpp + .h
(the 3 effect Tick()/Draw() splits with if(!ft) guards).
